28:["$","$L66",null,{"children":[["$","$L67",null,{"title":"Workers connect but never receive actions","id":"workers-connect-but-never-receive-actions","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Almost always the platform properties. Compare the keys the worker advertises\nagainst ",["$","code",null,{"children":"supported_platform_properties"}]," on the scheduler and against what the\nclient requests: a key the scheduler doesn't list can't be matched on, and a\nkey the worker doesn't advertise excludes it from anything requiring that key.\nCheck the scheduler log for the queue depth: actions queuing while workers\nidle is the signature."]}]}],["$","$L67",null,{"title":"`Object not found in either fast or slow store`","id":"object-not-found-in-either-fast-or-slow-store","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The worker cannot reach the blob through its ",["$","code",null,{"children":"slow"}]," store. Check that the\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"grpc"}]," store's address resolves from inside the worker (a container name that\nworks on the host network usually doesn't) and that the CAS server is the\nsame one the client uploaded to. This error also appears when the scheduler and\nthe workers point at different CAS servers."]}]}],["$","$L67",null,{"title":"Two workers on one host interfere with each other","id":"two-workers-on-one-host-interfere-with-each-other","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["They are sharing ",["$","code",null,{"children":"work_directory"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"content_path"}]," or ",["$","code",null,{"children":"temp_path"}],". The work\ndirectory is the worst of the three, because it is deleted and recreated at\nstartup: the second worker to start wipes the first one's in-flight actions.\nGive each process its own paths."]}]}],["$","$L67",null,{"title":"Adding workers made builds slower","id":"adding-workers-made-builds-slower","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["You have moved the bottleneck to the CAS server, which is now serving inputs to\nevery worker. Confirm by watching its network and disk while a build runs.\nRaising each worker's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast"}]," tier ",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_bytes"}]," cuts the read traffic; past that\nit is a CAS scaling problem."]}]}],["$","$L67",null,{"title":"Workers keep dropping and reconnecting","id":"workers-keep-dropping-and-reconnecting","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":["Check ",["$","code",null,{"children":"worker_api_endpoint.timeout"}]," on the worker against ",["$","code",null,{"children":"worker_timeout_s"}],"\non the scheduler, and any proxy or load balancer between the two. The worker\nsends a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"KeepAlive"}]," RPC every ",["$","code",null,{"children":"timeout / 2"}]," (default timeout 5 seconds), and\nthe scheduler evicts a worker it has not heard from within ",["$","code",null,{"children":"worker_timeout_s"}],"\n(default 10 seconds), so a hop that delays or drops those RPCs looks like a\nflapping worker. HTTP/2 keepalive pings on this listener come from\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"advanced_http.http2_keep_alive_interval"}]," on the scheduler's worker API\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"servers"}]," entry. The worker API is a long-lived streaming connection, not a\nseries of requests."]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-worker/src/local_worker.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-worker/src/local_worker.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-worker/src/local_worker.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":["$L68","start_keep_alive"]}]]}],"$L69"]}]
